commits.body:
The brief's Progress gains the for-review list Phase 5 step 5 asks for, at uwuktzll.

Tier A: each gate's state, with its commits and job ids. A0-A7 pass on the merged line. A8's offline part passes. Its two jobs decide the rest: 20261115-015944 (the 42 packet tasks and 7 native run paths with JBMC absent) and 20261115-020015 (28 constructed run paths). At writing, 020015 had finished passed but wasn't collected, and 015944 was running.

The portfolio in counts:
- 13 catalog-only entries;
- the six deep targets, all reproducible scaffolds. 285-287 and 306 are on published original JARs. 305 and 307 are source slices byte-matched to Spring's published classes on one side, partial at the exact commits' original-bytecode scope;
- all six attempted, with no claim of theirs closed;
- 105 with 3 of its 4 claims closed (one established, two refuted at pow(-2, 31)).

The 28 claim tasks are 1 proved, 2 refuted, 21 unresolved and 4 not executed, with what each scope permits concluding. Also listed: the five observed gaps (25 obligations, examples/gap-inventory.md), the pending jobs, timebox deferrals (none), what is for the user (four allow-list proposals, the stream directories, a push), and the review items gathered across the run.

The status is now waiting on the two A8 jobs. When both are collected and pass, Tier A passes and the brief is done.

Out of date in the brief, outside Progress: the Streams section's 4 GB per stream predates the 12G caps. Where it starts from is a recount at a7abc155, kept as recorded.
